1
00:00:00,834 --> 00:00:06,840
[theme music playing]

2
00:00:11,052 --> 00:00:13,638
[Emilia] <i>I promise to continue getting rid</i>

3
00:00:13,722 --> 00:00:16,474
<i>of the evil in our town.</i>

4
00:00:16,558 --> 00:00:18,977
<i>They're willing to take anyone</i>
<i>down just to clear their name.</i>

5
00:00:19,060 --> 00:00:21,104
<i>So don't mingle with those devils.</i>

6
00:00:21,187 --> 00:00:23,273
<i>How will I get justice for my family</i>

7
00:00:23,356 --> 00:00:25,066
<i>if I act like a coward?</i>

8
00:00:25,150 --> 00:00:29,654
<i>For my first project,</i>
<i>let me introduce to you</i>

9
00:00:29,738 --> 00:00:34,117
<i>a good friend of mine, Miss Ivy Aguas!</i>

10
00:00:34,200 --> 00:00:38,163
<i>I see that you're still siding</i>
<i>with the Ardientes, Senator.</i>

11
00:00:38,246 --> 00:00:40,081
<i>What's your game, Miss Aguas?</i>

12
00:00:40,165 --> 00:00:41,583
<i>If I tell you,</i>

13
00:00:41,666 --> 00:00:43,960
<i>you might not want</i>
<i>to play anymore, Senator.</i>

14
00:00:44,043 --> 00:00:46,337
<i>Maybe you can promote me in our party</i>

15
00:00:46,421 --> 00:00:48,298
<i>as a replacement candidate for Papa.</i>

16
00:00:48,381 --> 00:00:52,093
<i>I knew it. Your friendship</i>
<i>comes with a price.</i>

17
00:00:52,177 --> 00:00:54,763
<i>If you can't reach Julio's</i>
<i>level of influence,</i>

18
00:00:54,846 --> 00:00:56,556
<i>you'll only be wasting time and money</i>

19
00:00:56,639 --> 00:00:58,016
<i>because you'll surely lose.</i>

20
00:00:58,099 --> 00:01:01,561
<i>Jasmin's gone. I've searched</i>
<i>the whole house for her.</i>

21
00:01:01,644 --> 00:01:04,689
<i>Auntie, didn't I ask you</i>
<i>to keep an eye on her?</i>

22
00:01:04,773 --> 00:01:07,859
<i>Hi, Mr. Torillo. You look tense.</i>

23
00:01:07,942 --> 00:01:10,612
<i>Some of my men are stealing from me.</i>

24
00:01:10,695 --> 00:01:11,863
<i>You better be careful.</i>

25
00:01:11,946 --> 00:01:14,449
<i>-Ivy?</i>
<i>-Your son likes her.</i>

26
00:01:14,532 --> 00:01:16,951
<i>I'm not interested in that woman.</i>

27
00:01:17,035 --> 00:01:18,661
<i>You all need to vacate this property.</i>

28
00:01:18,745 --> 00:01:22,415
<i>I don't think this is right.</i>
<i>What about our livelihood?</i>

29
00:01:22,499 --> 00:01:24,000
<i>You know, this is useless!</i>

30
00:01:24,083 --> 00:01:25,752
<i>We've already issued an eviction notice!</i>

31
00:01:25,835 --> 00:01:28,338
<i>You don't have to side with them on this!</i>

32
00:01:28,421 --> 00:01:29,589
<i>If you'd only hear them out,</i>

33
00:01:29,672 --> 00:01:31,716
<i>you'd understand that</i>
<i>what you're doing is wrong.</i>

34
00:01:31,800 --> 00:01:33,676
[Emilia] <i>You're wasting my time. Leave.</i>

35
00:01:33,760 --> 00:01:35,345
<i>-Mom.</i>
<i>-Leave!</i>

36
00:01:41,768 --> 00:01:42,852
[Raul] Diego!

37
00:01:48,149 --> 00:01:51,277
What do you need? Maybe I can help.

38
00:01:52,529 --> 00:01:53,571
Nothing, Dad.

39
00:01:54,405 --> 00:01:56,032
I'm sorry, but you can't help me.

40
00:01:56,825 --> 00:01:58,243
You're leaving anyway, right?

41
00:01:59,035 --> 00:02:01,329
I'm leaving, all right.
I really want to go,

42
00:02:01,412 --> 00:02:03,706
but I want you to know
that the only reason

43
00:02:03,790 --> 00:02:06,793
I keep coming back here is because of you.

44
00:02:08,169 --> 00:02:11,339
Never forget that I'm on your side.

45
00:02:12,048 --> 00:02:13,341
I hope so, Dad.

46
00:02:24,394 --> 00:02:27,689
-It's really slippery here.
-So then, all is set.

47
00:02:27,939 --> 00:02:32,193
Mr. Fernan, Mr. Ramon, I trust
you can unite the farmers.

48
00:02:32,277 --> 00:02:36,573
Tell them to cooperate
to avoid any trouble.

49
00:02:36,656 --> 00:02:37,782
-Yes, Mayor.
-Yes, Mayor.

50
00:02:39,576 --> 00:02:40,618
Hey, Diego!

51
00:02:41,161 --> 00:02:42,620
What are you doing here, Arnaldo?

52
00:02:43,496 --> 00:02:45,373
We just settled some things for the EPZ.

53
00:02:45,456 --> 00:02:48,418
The mayor already gave
the notice of eviction.

54
00:02:48,501 --> 00:02:49,878
It's a month from today.

55
00:02:49,961 --> 00:02:51,045
What?

56
00:02:51,296 --> 00:02:53,298
Arnaldo, you can't do this!

57
00:02:53,631 --> 00:02:56,092
There's no point fighting. It's done.

58
00:02:56,175 --> 00:02:58,344
Everything's finalized. Just accept it.

59
00:03:05,101 --> 00:03:07,395
[Fernan] Careful, Miss Ivy! It's slippery.

60
00:03:07,478 --> 00:03:09,772
It just rained.

61
00:03:13,151 --> 00:03:16,154
[Arnaldo] Ivy, can you manage?
Ivy! Careful!

62
00:03:17,322 --> 00:03:18,406
-Thank you.
-[Fernan] Be careful, Miss Ivy.

63
00:03:18,489 --> 00:03:19,574
-It's slippery.
-Hold on to me.

64
00:03:19,657 --> 00:03:24,662
[romantic music playing]

65
00:03:30,543 --> 00:03:32,170
Oh, thank you.

66
00:03:34,714 --> 00:03:36,049
-Thank you, Mr. Mayor.
-Sure.

67
00:03:36,132 --> 00:03:37,717
Yeah. I'm okay. Let's go?

68
00:03:39,052 --> 00:03:41,221
-Oh!
-Hey! Hey!

69
00:03:42,764 --> 00:03:44,682
-Oh, no!
-Watch out!

70
00:03:44,933 --> 00:03:50,897
["Sa'Yo" by Silent Sanctuary playing]

71
00:03:59,280 --> 00:04:01,783
-Hold on. Careful.
-Um…

72
00:04:02,158 --> 00:04:03,493
Give me your hand.

73
00:04:05,620 --> 00:04:07,664
-I'm okay.
-You need to change, though.

74
00:04:07,747 --> 00:04:11,376
No, no, I'm okay.
I'll just change at home.

75
00:04:11,793 --> 00:04:13,461
You can change at Auntie Loring's.

76
00:04:13,544 --> 00:04:15,088
No need. Ivy wants to go home now.

77
00:04:15,171 --> 00:04:17,006
It's close by. You can wash there, too.

78
00:04:17,090 --> 00:04:20,093
-No. Thank you, Mr. Torillo.
-Oh, no! Careful!

79
00:04:20,176 --> 00:04:21,344
Come on. It won't take long.

80
00:04:21,427 --> 00:04:24,097
-Hey! Why are you so stubborn?!
-[shrieking]

81
00:04:24,180 --> 00:04:25,640
-Diego!
-It won't take long!

82
00:04:25,723 --> 00:04:28,017
Mr. Torillo, put me down!

83
00:04:28,101 --> 00:04:30,770
-You need to clean yourself up.
-What is your brother doing?

84
00:04:30,853 --> 00:04:34,148
[Diego] I'm only helping you,
so stop complaining.

85
00:04:35,775 --> 00:04:37,568
Thank you so much for the goodies.

86
00:04:37,652 --> 00:04:40,571
Yeah. Thank you, friend. Thank you.

87
00:04:46,202 --> 00:04:51,207
[soft tense music playing]

88
00:04:56,170 --> 00:04:57,338
Aww.

89
00:04:57,797 --> 00:05:00,633
The thing is, those aren't my favorites.

90
00:05:00,717 --> 00:05:02,093
Wildflowers?

91
00:05:02,176 --> 00:05:05,930
It's so barbaric, untamed, uncivilized.

92
00:05:07,473 --> 00:05:08,474
[Emilia sighs]

93
00:05:10,226 --> 00:05:11,477
Come on, Emilia.

94
00:05:11,561 --> 00:05:16,107
Let me ask you. Since you got
rid of Dante Cruz's family…

95
00:05:16,983 --> 00:05:20,236
do you remember any instances
or heard any rumors

96
00:05:20,320 --> 00:05:22,613
that I've womanized again?

97
00:05:22,697 --> 00:05:23,781
You haven't, right?

98
00:05:24,991 --> 00:05:28,202
So, please, don't be so cold.

99
00:05:28,745 --> 00:05:31,080
Especially now that
our anniversary's coming up.

100
00:05:32,832 --> 00:05:35,335
Wow, you actually remembered.
That's a miracle.

101
00:05:39,297 --> 00:05:40,548
Nanny!

102
00:05:40,882 --> 00:05:43,384
Can I have a vase for these flowers?

103
00:05:48,222 --> 00:05:50,641
But before anything else,

104
00:05:50,725 --> 00:05:52,769
I need to go to San Ildefonso.

105
00:05:52,852 --> 00:05:56,439
They have game fowl over there.

106
00:05:56,856 --> 00:05:58,357
I'm thinking of buying some

107
00:05:58,441 --> 00:06:00,401
since they'll do well for business.

108
00:06:01,110 --> 00:06:02,695
San Ildefonso? That far?

109
00:06:02,779 --> 00:06:04,822
I'll be back right away.

110
00:06:04,906 --> 00:06:06,783
In time for our anniversary.

111
00:06:07,241 --> 00:06:11,162
Emilia, I'll make sure we'll get
to celebrate our anniversary.

112
00:06:12,955 --> 00:06:16,417
Nanny! Where's the vase I asked for?

113
00:06:17,251 --> 00:06:18,252
[Emilia sighs]

114
00:06:20,379 --> 00:06:22,381
[Emilia humming]

115
00:06:29,764 --> 00:06:32,225
[Emilia humming]

116
00:06:34,310 --> 00:06:37,647
Miss Ivy, you can get dressed here.

117
00:06:38,815 --> 00:06:42,110
I'm sorry. It's a bit cramped.

118
00:06:43,152 --> 00:06:44,237
It's fine.

119
00:06:44,320 --> 00:06:47,907
I hope you're okay with
these clothes we borrowed.

120
00:06:48,950 --> 00:06:50,701
They're great, thanks.

121
00:06:52,995 --> 00:06:54,288
Miss Loring?

122
00:06:54,705 --> 00:06:59,544
I'm sorry we had to be
the bearer of bad news earlier.

123
00:06:59,627 --> 00:07:04,132
But thank you because you still
welcomed us and helped me out.

124
00:07:04,882 --> 00:07:05,967
It's okay.

125
00:07:07,510 --> 00:07:11,973
I also apologize for coming off
a bit rude earlier.

126
00:07:13,182 --> 00:07:14,434
It's fine.

127
00:07:14,767 --> 00:07:17,311
Believe it or not…

128
00:07:18,187 --> 00:07:19,856
I do understand.

129
00:07:22,525 --> 00:07:25,695
Please, go ahead and change.
I'll leave you to it.

130
00:07:25,778 --> 00:07:26,612
All right.

131
00:07:33,703 --> 00:07:35,121
I didn't like what you did earlier.

132
00:07:35,997 --> 00:07:37,623
Did I do something wrong?

133
00:07:37,874 --> 00:07:39,584
I even helped her out.

134
00:07:39,667 --> 00:07:41,335
What a priss.

135
00:07:41,419 --> 00:07:43,379
You know what I mean.

136
00:07:43,463 --> 00:07:46,424
What's mine is mine.
What's yours is yours.

137
00:07:47,717 --> 00:07:48,968
And Natalie?

138
00:07:49,385 --> 00:07:50,803
Isn't she your girlfriend?

139
00:07:51,554 --> 00:07:53,931
Arnaldo, if you always got
what you wanted back then,

140
00:07:54,474 --> 00:07:55,600
it won't happen this time.

141
00:07:56,684 --> 00:07:57,977
What do you mean?

142
00:07:59,061 --> 00:08:00,563
Ivy doesn't like you.

143
00:08:00,646 --> 00:08:03,774
She's just using you. Both you and Mom.

144
00:08:04,192 --> 00:08:08,654
And that's the reason
why I will never like her.

145
00:08:13,659 --> 00:08:19,665
["Sa'Yo" by Silent Sanctuary playing]

146
00:08:53,282 --> 00:08:55,451
-[screams]
-Oh!

147
00:08:56,786 --> 00:08:58,454
-Miss Aguas, I'm sorry!
-My god!

148
00:08:58,538 --> 00:09:00,957
Mr. Torillo, what were you doing?

149
00:09:01,040 --> 00:09:04,043
-Why were you peeping on me?
-I'm sorry! I didn't mean it!

150
00:09:04,126 --> 00:09:06,045
You didn't mean it?!

151
00:09:06,128 --> 00:09:08,256
Miss Aguas, I didn't know. I'm sorry.

152
00:09:08,339 --> 00:09:10,758
-How dare you peep on me!
-I'm sorry! Come on!

153
00:09:10,841 --> 00:09:13,261
-Sorry?!
-Sorry. Ow! That hurts!

154
00:09:13,344 --> 00:09:14,512
-I don't accept it!
-It hurts!

155
00:09:14,595 --> 00:09:16,889
-Why did you peep on me?!
-I wasn't peeping!

156
00:09:16,973 --> 00:09:18,599
You did! What else can you call that?

157
00:09:18,683 --> 00:09:20,643
I didn't peep on you.
I was going to my room.

158
00:09:21,477 --> 00:09:23,688
-Okay, fine! Sorry!
-Ouch! Hey!

159
00:09:23,771 --> 00:09:28,401
So your eyes just unconsciously
ran over my body, is that it?

160
00:09:29,110 --> 00:09:32,697
[laughing] Hey, Butchoy!

161
00:09:32,780 --> 00:09:34,198
That looks good.

162
00:09:34,282 --> 00:09:36,534
Looks like you ate all my cooking, too.

163
00:09:36,617 --> 00:09:38,077
Should I make some more?

164
00:09:38,160 --> 00:09:39,620
It's really good, Miss Loring!

165
00:09:39,704 --> 00:09:43,332
Your banana fritters are
the best! They're perfect!

166
00:09:43,416 --> 00:09:44,542
[laughs]

167
00:09:44,625 --> 00:09:47,837
Oh, you flatter me!

168
00:09:47,920 --> 00:09:50,131
I'll get you some water to wash it down.

169
00:09:50,214 --> 00:09:51,757
I'll do it, Miss Loring!

170
00:09:51,841 --> 00:09:55,845
You're just trying to get more
food, aren't you? [chuckles]

171
00:09:57,513 --> 00:09:59,140
Mayor, are you okay?

172
00:10:00,016 --> 00:10:00,975
[Loring chuckles softly]

173
00:10:01,058 --> 00:10:02,768
-Well?!
-I didn't mean it!

174
00:10:02,852 --> 00:10:05,438
So you admit that you peeped on me!

175
00:10:05,521 --> 00:10:06,814
Ouch, it hurts!

176
00:10:06,897 --> 00:10:08,983
How should I know you were in there?!

177
00:10:09,317 --> 00:10:11,027
-You peeped on me!
-That hurts! Hey!

178
00:10:11,110 --> 00:10:14,822
Diego. Miss Beautiful.
What are you two doing?

179
00:10:14,905 --> 00:10:20,911
["Sa'Yo" by Silent Sanctuary playing]

180
00:10:35,051 --> 00:10:38,179
-Uh, miss–
-Miss Loring, we have a winner!

181
00:10:38,262 --> 00:10:39,972
A winner? What winner?

182
00:10:40,056 --> 00:10:44,268
Um, Miss Loring, thanks again.
I have to go.

183
00:10:44,685 --> 00:10:45,811
Miss Aguas.

184
00:10:50,858 --> 00:10:52,610
It's okay, I'll get it.

185
00:10:52,693 --> 00:10:54,111
I'm sorry about what happened.

186
00:11:03,537 --> 00:11:04,580
Let's go.

187
00:11:05,665 --> 00:11:06,916
Mayor, Miss Ivy.

188
00:11:06,999 --> 00:11:08,876
Why don't you eat with us
before you leave?

189
00:11:08,959 --> 00:11:10,252
-That's right, Mayor.
-Yeah.

190
00:11:10,336 --> 00:11:11,504
I agree.

191
00:11:11,587 --> 00:11:16,759
It's a tradition here to hold
a feast after every harvest.

192
00:11:16,842 --> 00:11:18,886
Uh, I don't think it's necessary,

193
00:11:18,969 --> 00:11:21,222
but thank you for the time.
We'll be going now.

194
00:11:21,639 --> 00:11:22,890
Miss Beautiful.

195
00:11:23,724 --> 00:11:25,518
When are you coming back?

196
00:11:28,854 --> 00:11:31,107
Not anytime soon, Butchoy. Why?

197
00:11:31,190 --> 00:11:34,235
So we won't see each other
for a while then?

198
00:11:36,695 --> 00:11:38,155
Something like that.

199
00:11:38,239 --> 00:11:41,450
Then stay and eat with us.

200
00:11:41,534 --> 00:11:44,203
Please, Miss Beautiful.

201
00:11:44,286 --> 00:11:45,830
I'm going to miss you.

202
00:11:45,913 --> 00:11:48,833
[crowd chuckling]

203
00:11:48,916 --> 00:11:50,793
-[Fernan] Stay for a while.
-It's up to you.

204
00:11:54,046 --> 00:11:55,131
Okay, Butchoy.

205
00:11:55,214 --> 00:11:58,092
Yay! Miss Beautiful is staying! Yay!

206
00:11:58,175 --> 00:12:01,220
[chuckling]

207
00:12:01,303 --> 00:12:04,557
[Loring] There you go.
Miss Beautiful's staying.

208
00:12:04,640 --> 00:12:05,808
[Butchoy] Yay!

209
00:12:06,809 --> 00:12:07,977
[Emilia] Raul.

210
00:12:08,060 --> 00:12:10,646
Our charity event is in two weeks' time.

211
00:12:11,272 --> 00:12:13,107
You have to be back by then.

212
00:12:13,691 --> 00:12:18,446
And people should see us
together more often in public.

213
00:12:18,779 --> 00:12:21,157
I know. Besides, we'll go out next week.

214
00:12:21,240 --> 00:12:24,785
And I told you, I'll be back
for our anniversary.

215
00:12:25,703 --> 00:12:26,912
If you say so.

216
00:12:26,996 --> 00:12:32,001
[ominous music playing]

217
00:12:43,804 --> 00:12:44,889
[line rings]

218
00:12:44,972 --> 00:12:47,308
Hello, Mayor Mendoza?

219
00:12:47,391 --> 00:12:48,642
Yes.

220
00:12:48,726 --> 00:12:51,687
Raul is on his way to Ildefonso.

221
00:12:51,770 --> 00:12:53,439
I won't be there with him.

222
00:12:53,522 --> 00:12:56,192
Besides, he'll be there for business.

223
00:12:56,275 --> 00:12:58,402
Can you make sure you receive him well?

224
00:12:58,903 --> 00:12:59,987
Thanks.

225
00:13:01,655 --> 00:13:06,660
[ominous music playing]

226
00:13:09,580 --> 00:13:13,083
-Look at all the food!
-There we go!

227
00:13:13,167 --> 00:13:16,629
Nanny, add some more tomatoes here.

228
00:13:16,712 --> 00:13:18,214
-Mayor!
-There's so much food.

229
00:13:18,297 --> 00:13:19,632
Miss Ivy!

230
00:13:19,715 --> 00:13:22,218
Sit here. Come on!

231
00:13:22,426 --> 00:13:26,055
-Come here!
-Let's sit here.

232
00:13:26,138 --> 00:13:28,599
-Sit with us.
-Take your seats.

233
00:13:28,682 --> 00:13:31,685
Miss Beautiful, sit beside me.

234
00:13:31,769 --> 00:13:34,688
[chuckles] All right. I'll sit beside you.

235
00:13:36,273 --> 00:13:38,359
All right, then. Let's settle down.

236
00:13:38,442 --> 00:13:40,903
We don't have any utensils.
Where can I wash my hands?

237
00:13:40,986 --> 00:13:42,696
[chuckling]

238
00:13:42,780 --> 00:13:47,076
Mayor, it's a boodle fight.
We just gobble up.

239
00:13:47,159 --> 00:13:50,496
But if you have to, you can wash here.

240
00:13:50,579 --> 00:13:53,249
We also have one over there.

241
00:13:53,332 --> 00:13:55,751
-Let's wash our hands first.
-That's right.

242
00:13:55,834 --> 00:13:57,878
-Let's wash first.
-Here.

243
00:13:57,962 --> 00:14:02,967
[romantic music playing]

244
00:14:04,760 --> 00:14:08,347
-Mayor, for Miss Ivy.
-Let's go over there. Come on.

245
00:14:08,430 --> 00:14:09,765
-Miss Aguas.
-Miss Aguas.

246
00:14:11,433 --> 00:14:16,397
[romantic music continues playing]

247
00:14:22,611 --> 00:14:23,863
Give me that.

248
00:14:26,031 --> 00:14:27,241
Here, Miss Beautiful.

249
00:14:29,201 --> 00:14:30,369
Thank you, Butchoy.

250
00:14:30,619 --> 00:14:32,955
[Loring] All right, sirs….

251
00:14:33,038 --> 00:14:34,999
[Ivy] You go wash, too.

252
00:14:35,082 --> 00:14:37,459
[Loring] All right. Before we start.

253
00:14:38,043 --> 00:14:40,004
Here, Fernan.

254
00:14:40,713 --> 00:14:41,672
Okay?

255
00:14:41,755 --> 00:14:43,757
Nanny, where's Uncle Pandoy?

256
00:14:43,841 --> 00:14:45,467
Oh! He'll catch up later.

257
00:14:45,551 --> 00:14:47,386
He has something to take care of.

258
00:14:47,469 --> 00:14:49,763
Get some food. Don't be shy.

259
00:14:49,847 --> 00:14:50,973
-Diego?
-All right.

260
00:14:51,056 --> 00:14:53,851
Do you want me to get you some shrimp?

261
00:14:54,602 --> 00:14:56,395
I'm fine, Nimfa. Thank you.

262
00:14:56,478 --> 00:14:57,479
Sure.

263
00:15:03,652 --> 00:15:05,195
Here, Butchoy.

264
00:15:05,487 --> 00:15:08,824
Hey, why don't you have more food?

265
00:15:08,908 --> 00:15:10,826
I'm trying to lose weight,

266
00:15:10,910 --> 00:15:14,830
so my playmates will stop bullying me.

267
00:15:15,581 --> 00:15:17,833
Your playmates bully you?

268
00:15:20,210 --> 00:15:22,963
Here, have some more.

269
00:15:23,505 --> 00:15:26,717
You know, you shouldn't
let them bully you.

270
00:15:26,800 --> 00:15:30,179
They might get used to it.

271
00:15:30,262 --> 00:15:33,682
But how do I fight them? Do I sit on them?

272
00:15:33,766 --> 00:15:36,018
[chuckling]

273
00:15:36,101 --> 00:15:38,354
-Butchoy.
-Oh, that boy.

274
00:15:38,437 --> 00:15:39,939
If only you could.

275
00:15:40,356 --> 00:15:42,232
But of course, you can't do that.

276
00:15:42,316 --> 00:15:46,695
You should tell them that
what they're doing is wrong.

277
00:15:46,779 --> 00:15:49,156
On your end, try to be more active.

278
00:15:49,657 --> 00:15:52,785
You know what?
When Miss Beautiful has time…

279
00:15:53,494 --> 00:15:55,037
I'll exercise with you.

280
00:15:55,371 --> 00:15:56,789
[Butchoy] You will?

281
00:15:57,498 --> 00:15:59,041
I can't wait!

282
00:15:59,458 --> 00:16:01,710
-Okay, Miss Beautiful!
-[chuckles]

283
00:16:01,794 --> 00:16:03,379
["Sa'Yo" by Silent Sanctuary playing]

284
00:16:03,462 --> 00:16:06,715
<i>I'll help you not gain weight</i>
<i>even if you eat a lot!</i>

285
00:16:06,799 --> 00:16:10,844
<i>Go, Diego! Keep running!</i>
<i>I knew you could do it!</i>

286
00:16:10,928 --> 00:16:13,847
<i>It was hard, but you did it!</i>

287
00:16:16,809 --> 00:16:18,310
All right. Now, eat up.

288
00:16:19,311 --> 00:16:22,314
[Loring] He's like Diego
when he was younger.

289
00:16:22,398 --> 00:16:23,941
He used to eat everything!

290
00:16:24,024 --> 00:16:27,528
Banana fritters,
and especially a huge roast.

291
00:16:27,611 --> 00:16:29,113
[laughing]

292
00:16:29,196 --> 00:16:32,408
-Nanny, don't embarrass me.
-But it's true!

293
00:16:32,491 --> 00:16:35,536
But look at him now. I'm proud of him.

294
00:16:35,619 --> 00:16:37,621
Just look at his body!

295
00:16:37,705 --> 00:16:40,791
That's because his best friend
taught him how to exercise.

296
00:16:41,792 --> 00:16:43,752
Who's his best friend?

297
00:16:48,757 --> 00:16:50,759
[scoffs] Obviously, me.

298
00:16:51,760 --> 00:16:54,471
After all, I'm Diego's
only best friend here.

299
00:16:54,555 --> 00:16:56,724
We grew up in Ardiente together.

300
00:16:56,807 --> 00:16:58,392
We both studied in Manila

301
00:16:58,475 --> 00:17:01,020
and returned to Ardiente together.

302
00:17:01,103 --> 00:17:03,397
[Loring chuckles]

303
00:17:03,480 --> 00:17:10,404
You've been best friends
since you were kids, Nimfa?

304
00:17:11,822 --> 00:17:12,990
Uh…

305
00:17:13,699 --> 00:17:16,452
The truth is, Miss Ivy…

306
00:17:17,119 --> 00:17:19,204
We only became friends during high school.

307
00:17:19,288 --> 00:17:22,166
[Loring laughs] That's true.

308
00:17:22,249 --> 00:17:26,962
When Diego was a kid,
he had only one best friend,

309
00:17:27,046 --> 00:17:29,923
and she was his one and only true love.

310
00:17:30,007 --> 00:17:31,592
[teasing]

311
00:17:31,675 --> 00:17:33,469
Here we go!

312
00:17:33,552 --> 00:17:34,803
There you go again, Nanny.

313
00:17:34,887 --> 00:17:36,764
Why are you blushing?

314
00:17:36,847 --> 00:17:38,932
-[laughing]
-Seriously, Diego?

315
00:17:39,016 --> 00:17:41,435
That was so long ago.
You still think about her?

316
00:17:45,355 --> 00:17:47,733
What's her name, Diego?

317
00:17:49,610 --> 00:17:50,736
Uh…

318
00:17:53,447 --> 00:17:54,364
Lily.

319
00:17:58,035 --> 00:17:59,578
Her name is Lily.

320
00:17:59,661 --> 00:18:02,664
["Sa'Yo" by Silent Sanctuary playing]

321
00:18:04,458 --> 00:18:06,877
[Butchoy] Where's Lily now?

322
00:18:09,046 --> 00:18:10,380
Uh…

323
00:18:10,464 --> 00:18:13,133
Well, Lily left years ago.

324
00:18:15,010 --> 00:18:17,971
They never came back to Ardiente.

325
00:18:20,516 --> 00:18:22,643
I wonder where she is now.

326
00:18:26,688 --> 00:18:29,191
Let's stop talking about her, Miss Loring.

327
00:18:29,608 --> 00:18:33,654
I think the mayor and Miss Ivy
are getting bored

328
00:18:33,737 --> 00:18:35,948
listening to Diego talk about
his long-lost best friend.

329
00:18:36,031 --> 00:18:37,282
[Loring] Oh, I'm sorry.

330
00:18:37,366 --> 00:18:40,285
Besides, it's all in the past.
It should just stay there.

331
00:18:40,369 --> 00:18:41,370
Right?

332
00:18:43,080 --> 00:18:44,706
[Loring] Don't be shy. Eat some more.

333
00:18:55,843 --> 00:18:59,096
Um… Let me get that for you.

334
00:18:59,179 --> 00:19:01,557
I want you to keep eating.

335
00:19:01,640 --> 00:19:03,559
I don't want you to get hungry.

336
00:19:03,642 --> 00:19:05,269
There. You can eat it.

337
00:19:05,352 --> 00:19:07,563
Thank you, Miss Beautiful!

338
00:19:07,646 --> 00:19:08,647
Yummy!

339
00:19:08,730 --> 00:19:10,315
[chuckling]

340
00:19:10,399 --> 00:19:13,277
You're so cute!

341
00:19:13,360 --> 00:19:14,903
[chuckling]

342
00:19:17,948 --> 00:19:19,616
[young Lily] <i>You like it, huh?</i>

343
00:19:19,700 --> 00:19:22,452
<i>You're so cute! </i>[chuckles]

344
00:19:27,791 --> 00:19:29,793
[chuckling]

345
00:19:31,211 --> 00:19:36,133
[romantic music playing]

346
00:19:55,611 --> 00:19:58,864
Uh, ma'am, should I still serve
the meat roll?

347
00:19:58,947 --> 00:20:01,575
Are you sure you can
finish all that by yourself?

348
00:20:02,326 --> 00:20:04,119
Don't take the meat roll out.

349
00:20:04,203 --> 00:20:07,206
Take yourself out of this room instead!

350
00:20:07,289 --> 00:20:10,042
And don't come in until I say so.

351
00:20:10,125 --> 00:20:11,126
Sorry, ma'am.

352
00:20:12,669 --> 00:20:18,675
[tense music playing]

353
00:20:26,934 --> 00:20:27,935
Where is she?

354
00:20:35,525 --> 00:20:38,904
Jasmin, I was so worried
about you, so I rushed here.

355
00:20:39,780 --> 00:20:40,864
I'm sorry.

356
00:20:42,074 --> 00:20:44,660
I will stay with you until you get better.

357
00:20:58,632 --> 00:21:01,426
Uh, we should get going.

358
00:21:02,427 --> 00:21:05,681
Thank you so much for dinner.

359
00:21:05,764 --> 00:21:08,934
And Miss Loring, like what I said earlier,

360
00:21:09,017 --> 00:21:10,686
I'm really thankful.

361
00:21:10,769 --> 00:21:14,147
Even though we have our differences,

362
00:21:14,231 --> 00:21:16,900
you still welcomed us. Me and the mayor.

363
00:21:17,567 --> 00:21:20,028
[Fernan] That's how the people
of Ardiente are, Miss Ivy.

364
00:21:20,112 --> 00:21:23,365
We're always ready to lend a helping hand.

365
00:21:24,032 --> 00:21:27,286
All I want to say is we should
just trust our leaders.

366
00:21:27,619 --> 00:21:29,997
We won't do anything
that would harm the town.

367
00:21:30,080 --> 00:21:33,125
But the farmers have a right to be heard.

368
00:21:33,208 --> 00:21:35,877
I'll leave a request
for dialogue at your office,

369
00:21:35,961 --> 00:21:38,088
so you and Mom can listen to their side.

370
00:21:39,631 --> 00:21:42,801
Make sure you won't waste our time.

371
00:21:44,386 --> 00:21:45,637
What do you think, Ivy?

372
00:21:48,640 --> 00:21:51,810
Um… Mr. Mayor,
this will delay our project.

373
00:21:51,893 --> 00:21:53,812
[tense music playing]

374
00:21:54,980 --> 00:22:01,236
But maybe holding
a dialogue wouldn't hurt.

375
00:22:01,945 --> 00:22:03,572
I'll talk to the governor.

376
00:22:04,239 --> 00:22:06,408
I'll talk to your mother, Mr. Torillo.

377
00:22:07,367 --> 00:22:08,952
Thank you, Miss Aguas.

378
00:22:12,164 --> 00:22:14,416
All right. Thank you.

379
00:22:14,916 --> 00:22:16,084
[Fernan] Thank you, Mayor.

380
00:22:17,127 --> 00:22:18,211
[Loring] Thank you.

381
00:22:29,139 --> 00:22:31,516
[Raul] This will get better
soon. We just have to treat it.

382
00:22:45,822 --> 00:22:47,115
Don't worry.

383
00:22:48,116 --> 00:22:50,368
As long as I'm here, you'll be okay.

384
00:23:07,886 --> 00:23:10,472
Hello, Mayor Mendoza.

385
00:23:11,098 --> 00:23:12,808
Have you met up with Raul?

386
00:23:15,644 --> 00:23:18,897
Oh, yes. He mentioned he needs

387
00:23:18,980 --> 00:23:21,274
to do something first before meeting you.

388
00:23:21,817 --> 00:23:23,944
Maybe that's why he's not there.

389
00:23:24,861 --> 00:23:26,780
All right. Thanks, Mayor.

390
00:23:26,863 --> 00:23:29,533
I'll update you once I get hold of Raul.

391
00:23:29,866 --> 00:23:31,159
Thank you.

392
00:23:36,289 --> 00:23:38,750
[Emilia] A dialogue with those farmers?

393
00:23:40,043 --> 00:23:41,878
Why would I do that, Ivy?

394
00:23:41,962 --> 00:23:44,256
Besides, they'll be evicted soon.

395
00:23:44,756 --> 00:23:47,050
This is a necessary step, Emilia.

396
00:23:47,134 --> 00:23:48,760
In my business,

397
00:23:48,844 --> 00:23:52,097
this is how we check the
intricacies of land ownership.

398
00:23:52,180 --> 00:23:54,766
Sometimes, this is how we discover

399
00:23:54,850 --> 00:23:57,686
whether or not the property is viable.

400
00:23:59,396 --> 00:24:02,983
I hope those farmers
don't test my patience, Ivy.

401
00:24:03,984 --> 00:24:06,319
If this problem doesn't end…

402
00:24:06,903 --> 00:24:08,363
I'll end them myself.

403
00:24:27,215 --> 00:24:32,220
[dramatic music playing]

404
00:24:37,100 --> 00:24:38,685
1958?

405
00:24:40,145 --> 00:24:45,150
[unsettling music playing]

406
00:25:16,181 --> 00:25:21,144
[unsettling music continues playing]

407
00:25:35,200 --> 00:25:36,618
I knew it.

408
00:25:44,542 --> 00:25:46,002
Arnaldo, what is this?

409
00:25:46,795 --> 00:25:48,713
Why does this document state

410
00:25:48,797 --> 00:25:51,883
that the Ardientes don't own
the lot that you want?

411
00:25:51,967 --> 00:25:53,969
[tense music playing]

412
00:25:55,804 --> 00:25:57,931
Uncle Pandoy was right.

413
00:25:58,223 --> 00:26:01,559
Our ancestors gave the lot to the farmers.

414
00:26:01,643 --> 00:26:03,103
Who hid this? You?

415
00:26:03,687 --> 00:26:05,188
-[scoffs]
-Or Grandpa?

416
00:26:05,981 --> 00:26:07,232
First of all…

417
00:26:08,608 --> 00:26:10,652
Don't go through my things.

418
00:26:12,737 --> 00:26:15,740
Second, don't drag Grandpa
into your nonsense.

419
00:26:16,199 --> 00:26:18,618
-The farmers have a chance.
-Shut it.

420
00:26:19,119 --> 00:26:20,662
What will you do with this?

421
00:26:22,622 --> 00:26:24,291
Will you use it against your family?

422
00:26:27,419 --> 00:26:28,420
See?

423
00:26:29,796 --> 00:26:31,089
You can't do it.

424
00:26:34,634 --> 00:26:35,635
[gasps]

425
00:26:37,470 --> 00:26:41,474
[dramatic music playing]

426
00:26:42,726 --> 00:26:44,311
[Arnaldo] So let me get this straight.

427
00:26:44,769 --> 00:26:46,771
You made a promise to Diego?

428
00:26:46,855 --> 00:26:49,024
Don't worry about upsetting him.

429
00:26:49,107 --> 00:26:50,608
He's as harmless as a fish.

430
00:26:51,234 --> 00:26:52,652
It's about Emilia.

431
00:26:53,028 --> 00:26:54,612
Is she going through something?

432
00:26:55,155 --> 00:27:00,410
I just don't understand why she can't see

433
00:27:00,493 --> 00:27:03,747
that when explaining
these things to the farmers,

434
00:27:03,830 --> 00:27:05,790
we have to be patient.

435
00:27:05,874 --> 00:27:09,210
Well, that land rightfully
belongs to the Ardientes.

436
00:27:09,836 --> 00:27:11,254
And those farmers?

437
00:27:11,880 --> 00:27:14,424
Just push them out!

438
00:27:14,841 --> 00:27:19,804
Force them out and put up
a fence so they can't trespass.

439
00:27:20,138 --> 00:27:22,098
Well, it's not that easy, Natalie.

440
00:27:23,266 --> 00:27:24,642
There is a process.

441
00:27:24,726 --> 00:27:26,102
Oh, come on.

442
00:27:26,186 --> 00:27:29,356
We all know you're just
prolonging the process

443
00:27:29,439 --> 00:27:32,984
so you can spend more time
with my boyfriend. Am I right?

444
00:27:33,902 --> 00:27:35,779
I have no time for this.

445
00:27:36,237 --> 00:27:39,407
Don't you dare stand
while I'm still talking to you!

446
00:27:39,491 --> 00:27:41,826
Arnaldo, can you please
not bring your girlfriend

447
00:27:41,910 --> 00:27:43,787
to our next business meeting?

448
00:27:44,120 --> 00:27:45,622
You're a snake!

449
00:27:45,955 --> 00:27:48,333
A tease and cheap counterfeit--

450
00:27:49,292 --> 00:27:51,586
Don't try me, Natalie.

451
00:27:56,174 --> 00:27:57,342
[screams]

452
00:28:10,522 --> 00:28:15,527
[suspenseful music playing]

453
00:28:30,125 --> 00:28:31,167
Miss Aguas.

454
00:28:31,251 --> 00:28:32,460
Mr. Torillo.

455
00:28:35,213 --> 00:28:36,339
Good luck.

456
00:28:41,261 --> 00:28:42,554
Mr. Mayor.

457
00:28:50,437 --> 00:28:51,521
Shall we?

458
00:28:53,481 --> 00:28:55,608
Governor. Madam…

459
00:28:55,692 --> 00:28:57,318
The dialogue is about to start.

460
00:28:57,402 --> 00:28:59,654
Do you even think I have
the slightest interest

461
00:28:59,738 --> 00:29:01,156
for such nonsense?

462
00:29:01,239 --> 00:29:02,574
Let's go back to the mansion.

463
00:29:03,116 --> 00:29:05,201
Gov! Governor Emilia!

464
00:29:05,285 --> 00:29:06,369
Gov.

465
00:29:06,453 --> 00:29:08,788
We just want to let you know

466
00:29:08,872 --> 00:29:11,958
that we have full confidence
in your plans for our town.

467
00:29:12,751 --> 00:29:15,336
Is that so, Fernan? Thank you.

468
00:29:15,420 --> 00:29:16,713
Hello, Ramon.

469
00:29:16,796 --> 00:29:19,215
What are you waiting for? Let's go in.

470
00:29:19,966 --> 00:29:22,051
Let's go in, friends!

471
00:29:22,761 --> 00:29:25,555
-Thank you!
-Thank you, Governor!

472
00:29:27,932 --> 00:29:30,518
We do understand

473
00:29:30,602 --> 00:29:33,313
that you've been staying
on that land for a long time.

474
00:29:33,855 --> 00:29:39,277
That's why we will make sure
to relocate all of you.

475
00:29:39,778 --> 00:29:42,405
[Emilia] We'll also provide you
with sufficient funds

476
00:29:42,489 --> 00:29:44,324
so you can start over.

477
00:29:44,949 --> 00:29:47,076
WERE YOU ABLE TO FIND A WAY
TO GIVE THE DOCUMENT TO DIEGO?

478
00:29:47,160 --> 00:29:49,329
[Emilia] We only want the best for you.

479
00:29:49,412 --> 00:29:51,664
We want you all to have better lives

480
00:29:51,748 --> 00:29:54,375
because we truly care about you.

481
00:29:54,459 --> 00:29:55,668
[crowd murmuring]

482
00:29:55,752 --> 00:29:58,546
I PUT THE DOCUMENT
AMONG DIEGO'S THINGS.

483
00:29:58,630 --> 00:30:01,466
[crowd murmuring]

484
00:30:12,435 --> 00:30:13,311
Mom.

485
00:30:13,937 --> 00:30:15,230
Madam Governor.

486
00:30:17,106 --> 00:30:20,026
It's stated here that our ancestors

487
00:30:20,109 --> 00:30:21,945
gave that land to the farmers.

488
00:30:23,029 --> 00:30:24,447
[Emilia] Come on, Diego.

489
00:30:24,531 --> 00:30:26,616
That's just an old wives' tale.

490
00:30:26,699 --> 00:30:29,494
Only fools would believe in those rumors.

491
00:30:29,577 --> 00:30:31,579
But there is truth in every story.

492
00:30:42,215 --> 00:30:45,176
I only had to find out
that one piece of information

493
00:30:45,260 --> 00:30:48,888
to unearth what's been
kept secret from this town.

494
00:30:49,889 --> 00:30:51,015
Everyone.

495
00:30:51,724 --> 00:30:53,977
I have here an old draft,

496
00:30:54,060 --> 00:30:56,479
the deed of donation from 1958,

497
00:30:56,563 --> 00:30:59,691
confirming that the land
was donated to the farmers.

498
00:30:59,774 --> 00:31:04,779
[crowd murmuring, cheering]

499
00:31:15,748 --> 00:31:17,876
Friends, everyone.

500
00:31:21,004 --> 00:31:23,006
Diego, my son.

501
00:31:24,591 --> 00:31:27,343
Where and how did you get this?

502
00:31:27,427 --> 00:31:28,970
It wasn't even notarized.

503
00:31:31,639 --> 00:31:36,269
Diego, I know you have a heart
for the less fortunate.

504
00:31:36,519 --> 00:31:40,273
But do you really have to get
their hopes up for nothing?

505
00:31:41,566 --> 00:31:43,192
But isn't it worse

506
00:31:43,276 --> 00:31:46,362
to claim a property
that's rightfully theirs?

507
00:31:46,446 --> 00:31:49,282
To abuse their rights because
they've remained silent?

508
00:31:49,699 --> 00:31:52,076
Mom. Everything has its limits.

509
00:31:52,619 --> 00:31:54,203
Now, they've been given a voice.

510
00:31:54,454 --> 00:31:55,538
And they will fight!

511
00:31:55,622 --> 00:31:58,583
-We're going to fight!
-[crowd talking indistinctly]

512
00:32:02,170 --> 00:32:03,963
Please wait.

513
00:32:04,047 --> 00:32:05,506
Silence!

514
00:32:06,925 --> 00:32:08,092
[Fernan] Settle down.

515
00:32:08,885 --> 00:32:10,637
Friends.

516
00:32:11,804 --> 00:32:13,890
I am your governor.

517
00:32:14,432 --> 00:32:17,810
I'd never put any of you in harm's way.

518
00:32:18,519 --> 00:32:19,646
Don't worry.

519
00:32:20,021 --> 00:32:23,775
I will review this document
due to this new development.

520
00:32:24,943 --> 00:32:28,112
-[clapping]
-Thank you, Ma'am Emilia!

521
00:32:28,196 --> 00:32:30,865
You truly took after Señor Julio!

522
00:32:30,949 --> 00:32:33,117
Thank you so much!

523
00:32:33,201 --> 00:32:34,702
Thank you.

524
00:32:35,703 --> 00:32:38,081
Thank you very much.

525
00:32:40,249 --> 00:32:44,253
[dramatic music playing]

526
00:32:46,756 --> 00:32:49,634
[Fernan] Let's just wait for the result.

527
00:32:49,717 --> 00:32:51,469
We will wait.

528
00:32:51,552 --> 00:32:54,597
We still don't know
if the documents are valid.

529
00:32:54,681 --> 00:32:58,685
[indistinct chatter]

530
00:32:59,686 --> 00:33:01,854
[Fernan] Let's hear out the Ardientes.

531
00:33:03,106 --> 00:33:07,485
Let's wait for the result.

532
00:33:07,568 --> 00:33:09,237
Let's trust them.

533
00:33:13,908 --> 00:33:15,034
[indistinct chatter]

534
00:33:15,118 --> 00:33:18,162
Hey, Fernan. Ramon.

535
00:33:18,246 --> 00:33:19,831
Now, do you believe

536
00:33:19,914 --> 00:33:23,501
that the land was donated to us
by the Ardientes' ancestors?

537
00:33:23,584 --> 00:33:26,212
Good thing Diego has an ace up his sleeve.

538
00:33:26,295 --> 00:33:28,339
[giggles] Thank you, Diego, my love.

539
00:33:28,423 --> 00:33:31,426
-"My love"? What are you saying?
-[laughing]

540
00:33:31,509 --> 00:33:35,847
We should also thank
Gov. Emilia and Mayor Arnaldo

541
00:33:35,930 --> 00:33:38,558
for hearing us out.

542
00:33:39,434 --> 00:33:42,770
I was really surprised with Miss Ivy.

543
00:33:42,854 --> 00:33:44,439
She felt for us.

544
00:33:44,522 --> 00:33:50,361
She could've stayed silent
since she's an investor in EPZ,

545
00:33:50,820 --> 00:33:55,074
but she let us have a peaceful dialogue.

546
00:33:55,158 --> 00:33:56,492
Right, Diego?

547
00:33:58,578 --> 00:34:01,998
All right, Nanny. I'll talk to Ms. Aguas.

548
00:34:02,707 --> 00:34:04,917
Diego, thanks again.

549
00:34:05,501 --> 00:34:08,212
I hope your family finally realizes

550
00:34:08,296 --> 00:34:12,258
that they shouldn't belittle
Diego Ardiente-Torillo.

551
00:34:12,341 --> 00:34:13,968
[laughing and cheering]

552
00:34:14,052 --> 00:34:15,553
-Thank you.
-All right, everyone.

553
00:34:15,636 --> 00:34:16,929
Bye!

554
00:34:20,183 --> 00:34:21,684
Madrigal, you may go.

555
00:34:27,273 --> 00:34:28,524
So, you got what you wanted.

556
00:34:30,026 --> 00:34:31,569
When do I get my end of the bargain?

557
00:34:33,196 --> 00:34:34,363
Mr. Mayor…

558
00:34:35,782 --> 00:34:39,619
I'm one of the richest
women in the country.

559
00:34:40,620 --> 00:34:43,331
It's a shame if I only end up

560
00:34:43,414 --> 00:34:48,419
as a small town mayor's other woman.

561
00:34:51,130 --> 00:34:52,840
Touché, but…

562
00:34:52,924 --> 00:34:54,675
who says you're the other woman?

563
00:34:56,803 --> 00:34:58,763
You, Miss Aguas, are the only one.

564
00:34:58,846 --> 00:34:59,931
You're different.

565
00:35:00,431 --> 00:35:01,891
You're ruthless.

566
00:35:01,974 --> 00:35:04,393
Knows what she wants and gets it.

567
00:35:04,477 --> 00:35:06,020
But strangely…

568
00:35:07,313 --> 00:35:08,856
has a heart for the poor.

569
00:35:10,191 --> 00:35:11,400
I can't say for sure,

570
00:35:11,484 --> 00:35:17,406
but it's like the perfect
characteristics of a first lady.

571
00:35:18,407 --> 00:35:20,701
My first lady.

572
00:35:26,290 --> 00:35:28,668
You're the only woman who's
ever made me feel this way.

573
00:35:33,089 --> 00:35:36,050
And I'm sorry if I come
on strong, it's just that

574
00:35:36,134 --> 00:35:38,928
when I'm with you,
I forget about everything else.

575
00:35:39,804 --> 00:35:41,305
Mr. Mayor.

576
00:35:42,140 --> 00:35:43,558
I know that…

577
00:35:45,518 --> 00:35:47,395
you're only acting this way

578
00:35:47,478 --> 00:35:52,233
because that leech you
call a girlfriend isn't here.

579
00:35:53,651 --> 00:35:54,986
Am I right?

580
00:35:59,031 --> 00:36:01,033
Then I think we should
make the most out of it.

581
00:36:07,790 --> 00:36:09,041
[Diego] Miss Aguas, wait!

582
00:36:09,333 --> 00:36:10,418
Miss Aguas!

583
00:36:20,344 --> 00:36:21,596
Mr. Torillo.

584
00:36:26,851 --> 00:36:27,977
I'm sorry.

585
00:36:28,561 --> 00:36:30,229
I didn't mean to intrude.

586
00:36:30,313 --> 00:36:32,565
Are you referring to what you did earlier?

587
00:36:32,648 --> 00:36:35,109
[tense music playing]

588
00:36:35,193 --> 00:36:36,819
Aren't you ashamed of yourself?

589
00:36:36,903 --> 00:36:40,698
How dare you go against your own family?

590
00:36:40,781 --> 00:36:42,700
I'm not going against my family.

591
00:36:42,783 --> 00:36:46,704
I'm just letting you know about
the concerns of the farmers.

592
00:36:46,787 --> 00:36:50,124
You spend every day with them
and fight for their rights.

593
00:36:50,541 --> 00:36:54,003
Whether you admit it or not,
your actions and beliefs

594
00:36:54,086 --> 00:36:56,631
go against the Ardientes, your own family!

595
00:36:56,714 --> 00:36:58,633
Why can't you understand that?

596
00:36:58,716 --> 00:36:59,759
Mr. Mayor.

597
00:37:01,552 --> 00:37:03,512
What? Are you taking his side?

598
00:37:03,596 --> 00:37:04,597
No.

599
00:37:05,056 --> 00:37:07,683
But you shouldn't be fighting here.

600
00:37:08,517 --> 00:37:09,685
I don't care.

601
00:37:10,561 --> 00:37:12,980
If you pull this stunt again…

602
00:37:13,606 --> 00:37:15,316
you will answer to me.

603
00:37:15,775 --> 00:37:17,443
You will answer to me!

604
00:37:19,779 --> 00:37:21,072
Don't forget that.

605
00:37:22,740 --> 00:37:24,367
Mayor, is there a problem?

606
00:37:24,450 --> 00:37:29,455
[tense music playing]

607
00:37:43,219 --> 00:37:48,224
[soft dramatic music playing]

608
00:37:59,443 --> 00:38:01,445
[knocking on door]

609
00:38:01,529 --> 00:38:02,697
Raul?

610
00:38:08,703 --> 00:38:10,079
Hi, good evening, Madam Gov.

611
00:38:10,162 --> 00:38:11,998
I'm just bringing in the laundry.

612
00:38:13,416 --> 00:38:15,793
You again? If you're not
taking something out,

613
00:38:15,876 --> 00:38:17,378
you're bringing something in.

614
00:38:18,212 --> 00:38:21,799
What if I put your head
inside the comforter?!

615
00:38:21,966 --> 00:38:24,010
-Get out!
-I knocked on the door, madam.

616
00:38:24,093 --> 00:38:26,554
Stop talking! Get out of here!

617
00:38:37,231 --> 00:38:38,316
See.

618
00:38:40,526 --> 00:38:42,320
I told you it'd heal right away.

619
00:38:43,112 --> 00:38:44,488
I'll just clean it.

620
00:38:51,746 --> 00:38:52,955
You know what?

621
00:38:53,414 --> 00:38:56,542
Whenever I'm with Emilia…

622
00:38:57,918 --> 00:39:04,008
I feel like a slave who has to
satisfy their every whim.

623
00:39:05,634 --> 00:39:08,721
Not to mention, my father
was Julio's bodyguard.

624
00:39:09,263 --> 00:39:11,474
That's why they look down on me.

625
00:39:12,058 --> 00:39:16,937
They never made me feel accepted
as part of their family.

626
00:39:20,566 --> 00:39:24,195
But I know that someday,
I'll be as powerful as them.

627
00:39:30,785 --> 00:39:32,495
When that happens…

628
00:39:35,206 --> 00:39:36,999
I'll leave Emilia.

629
00:39:38,876 --> 00:39:40,836
And I'll choose you, Camia.

630
00:40:06,529 --> 00:40:07,655
All right, it's late.

631
00:40:08,030 --> 00:40:11,158
You should get some rest.

632
00:40:42,940 --> 00:40:43,983
Babe?

633
00:40:45,109 --> 00:40:46,735
Babe, what's up with you?

634
00:40:48,320 --> 00:40:53,325
[sensual music playing]

635
00:41:10,926 --> 00:41:12,553
You like it rough, huh?

636
00:41:21,312 --> 00:41:23,564
If only I could tell him everything…

637
00:41:24,857 --> 00:41:26,442
so he wouldn't think…

638
00:41:28,944 --> 00:41:30,863
that I'm like the rest of his family.

639
00:41:31,697 --> 00:41:33,073
But I can't.

640
00:41:34,033 --> 00:41:35,701
I can't risk it.

641
00:41:36,911 --> 00:41:37,995
It sounds like…

642
00:41:39,288 --> 00:41:43,918
Diego's opinion matters
a lot to you, dear.

643
00:41:47,755 --> 00:41:48,714
Hey, Diego.

644
00:41:48,797 --> 00:41:52,343
Did you go to Miss Ivy?
Were you able to thank her?

645
00:41:55,179 --> 00:41:57,223
Why should we thank her?

646
00:41:57,640 --> 00:42:00,434
-Huh?
-She's the reason for all this.

647
00:42:03,187 --> 00:42:05,439
-I tried to thank her, Nanny.
-And?

648
00:42:05,773 --> 00:42:06,899
But I couldn't…

649
00:42:09,568 --> 00:42:11,570
because she was with my brother.

650
00:42:11,654 --> 00:42:14,323
Aha! So that's why.

651
00:42:14,406 --> 00:42:18,827
-[Fernan chuckling]
-You got jealous.

652
00:42:19,787 --> 00:42:21,372
It's Diego.

653
00:42:22,373 --> 00:42:23,666
He's my childhood friend.

654
00:42:23,916 --> 00:42:26,168
We've been through a lot together.

655
00:42:28,837 --> 00:42:30,047
But the thing is…

656
00:42:33,092 --> 00:42:34,802
he doesn't know it's me.

657
00:42:36,220 --> 00:42:37,513
Maybe…

658
00:42:39,765 --> 00:42:42,810
you have feelings for him.

659
00:42:45,771 --> 00:42:46,897
[Fernan] Hold on.

660
00:42:46,981 --> 00:42:49,108
The mayor has a girlfriend, right?

661
00:42:49,191 --> 00:42:51,652
Then why is he always with Miss Ivy?

662
00:42:51,860 --> 00:42:53,279
You know, Diego…

663
00:42:53,821 --> 00:42:57,074
If you weren't so angry with Miss Ivy,

664
00:42:57,157 --> 00:42:59,243
I'd say you'd look good together.

665
00:43:01,287 --> 00:43:03,163
It would only ruin my plans.

666
00:43:04,081 --> 00:43:05,624
My dear…

667
00:43:05,708 --> 00:43:07,626
I know you're angry.

668
00:43:08,711 --> 00:43:10,504
But it doesn't mean you're heartless.

669
00:43:11,171 --> 00:43:12,965
Diego is a good man.

670
00:43:13,340 --> 00:43:15,718
You're fighting for the same thing.

671
00:43:16,135 --> 00:43:20,472
It's not wrong to open
your heart to someone, dear.

672
00:43:23,475 --> 00:43:25,185
Hey, hey, hey! Cut it out!

673
00:43:25,269 --> 00:43:26,812
He still has his Lily.

674
00:43:26,895 --> 00:43:29,315
-And Nimfa, too.
-[Loring] Whoa!

675
00:43:29,398 --> 00:43:33,193
[Fernan] Hey! You're too young for that.

676
00:43:33,444 --> 00:43:36,530
Fine, I'll thank her. But that's it.

677
00:43:37,448 --> 00:43:39,950
Because I will never fall for that woman.

678
00:43:40,534 --> 00:43:43,078
Is that so? Are you sure?

679
00:43:43,162 --> 00:43:46,373
-Look, your nose is growing!
-[laughing]

680
00:43:46,457 --> 00:43:48,334
At least try acting the part.

681
00:43:49,293 --> 00:43:50,753
You're right.

682
00:43:51,754 --> 00:43:53,505
Diego is a good man.

683
00:43:55,466 --> 00:43:56,884
That's why…

684
00:43:58,802 --> 00:44:01,680
I shouldn't drag him into my plans.

685
00:44:07,519 --> 00:44:09,521
-Why didn't you tell me?
-You okay?

686
00:44:09,605 --> 00:44:12,399
-You're playing and seek!
-You said it.

687
00:44:12,483 --> 00:44:14,610
-With your feelings!
-True!

688
00:44:14,693 --> 00:44:16,153
[laughing]

689
00:44:16,236 --> 00:44:17,446
-Cut it out!
-Look!

690
00:44:17,529 --> 00:44:21,367
-Your nose is growing longer.
-See? It's so long now.

691
00:44:27,164 --> 00:44:29,208
[Raul] <i>I need to go to San Ildefonso.</i>

692
00:44:29,291 --> 00:44:32,670
<i>I'll be back in time for our anniversary.</i>

693
00:44:35,714 --> 00:44:36,924
[Emilia] <i>Mayor Mendoza.</i>

694
00:44:37,007 --> 00:44:38,967
<i>Have you met up with Raul?</i>

695
00:44:39,051 --> 00:44:42,388
<i>Oh, yes. He mentioned that</i>
<i>he needs to do something first</i>

696
00:44:42,471 --> 00:44:44,682
<i>before meeting you.</i>

697
00:44:45,307 --> 00:44:47,434
<i>Maybe that's why he's not there.</i>

698
00:44:49,478 --> 00:44:50,687
[Raul] <i>Come on, Emilia.</i>

699
00:44:50,771 --> 00:44:54,400
<i>Since the time you got rid</i>
<i>of Dante Cruz's family,</i>

700
00:44:54,483 --> 00:44:57,820
<i>do you remember any rumors</i>
<i>that I've womanized again?</i>

701
00:44:57,903 --> 00:44:59,446
<i>You haven't, right?</i>

702
00:44:59,530 --> 00:45:02,199
Happy anniversary, my love.

703
00:45:02,908 --> 00:45:05,536
[sobbing]

704
00:45:05,619 --> 00:45:07,871
Happy anniversary, my love.

705
00:45:32,771 --> 00:45:35,482
Happy anniversary, my love.

706
00:45:35,566 --> 00:45:39,069
Happy anniversary? What's so happy? Happy?

707
00:45:39,153 --> 00:45:41,321
What's so happy?!

708
00:45:41,405 --> 00:45:43,115
I'm not happy!

709
00:45:48,162 --> 00:45:50,080
I'm not happy.

710
00:45:51,248 --> 00:45:55,252
[sobbing]

711
00:45:58,589 --> 00:46:03,594
[ominous music playing]

712
00:46:11,518 --> 00:46:12,728
Maid.

713
00:46:15,355 --> 00:46:16,982
Ma'am, do you need anything?

714
00:46:17,900 --> 00:46:19,318
Clean this up.

715
00:46:19,651 --> 00:46:22,905
I don't want to see a speck of dirt here

716
00:46:22,988 --> 00:46:24,448
when I wake up tomorrow.

717
00:46:24,740 --> 00:46:25,824
Yes, ma'am.

718
00:46:32,164 --> 00:46:37,169
[ominous music playing]

719
00:46:42,799 --> 00:46:47,804
["Sa'Yo" by Silent Sanctuary playing]

720
00:46:55,395 --> 00:46:56,605
<i>Lily.</i>

721
00:46:57,231 --> 00:46:59,233
<i>Thanks for helping me out.</i>

722
00:46:59,566 --> 00:47:01,693
<i>No worries! I got you.</i>

723
00:47:04,780 --> 00:47:07,366
[Loring] <i>I'm so proud of him.</i>
<i>Look at his body.</i>

724
00:47:07,449 --> 00:47:10,285
<i>His best friend taught him</i>
<i>how to exercise.</i>

725
00:47:10,369 --> 00:47:13,497
<i>And she was his one and only true love.</i>

726
00:47:13,580 --> 00:47:15,832
<i>What's her name, Diego?</i>

727
00:47:16,291 --> 00:47:17,334
<i>Lily.</i>

728
00:47:18,293 --> 00:47:19,795
<i>Her name is Lily.</i>

729
00:47:20,963 --> 00:47:25,968
["Sa'Yo" by Silent Sanctuary
continues playing]

730
00:47:36,728 --> 00:47:38,897
<i>Let me get that for you.</i>

731
00:47:39,773 --> 00:47:41,775
<i>You're so cute!</i>

732
00:47:52,494 --> 00:47:53,620
[Ivy] <i>It's Diego.</i>

733
00:47:53,704 --> 00:47:56,456
-<i>Don't jump! Hey!</i>
-[Ivy] <i>He's my childhood friend.</i>

734
00:47:57,457 --> 00:47:58,375
<i>Oh!</i>

735
00:47:59,835 --> 00:48:01,920
[Ivy] <i>We've been through a lot together.</i>

736
00:48:03,213 --> 00:48:08,010
[Carlotta] <i>Maybe you have</i>
<i>feelings for him.</i>

737
00:48:08,927 --> 00:48:10,804
<i>Diego's a good man.</i>

738
00:48:10,887 --> 00:48:15,100
<i>It's not wrong to open</i>
<i>your heart to someone.</i>

739
00:48:15,183 --> 00:48:19,313
["Sa'Yo" by Silent Sanctuary
continues playing]

740
00:48:19,396 --> 00:48:21,857
[Ivy] <i>What is this feeling?</i>

741
00:48:21,940 --> 00:48:23,400
<i>I'm confused.</i>

742
00:48:24,735 --> 00:48:28,614
<i>Am I holding on to the memories</i>
<i>of when we were still friends?</i>

743
00:48:31,575 --> 00:48:32,951
[Fernan] <i>You know, Diego?</i>

744
00:48:33,035 --> 00:48:36,872
<i>If you weren't so angry with Miss Ivy,</i>

745
00:48:36,955 --> 00:48:38,373
<i>you'd look good together.</i>

746
00:48:38,457 --> 00:48:40,167
-[screams]
-<i>Oh!</i>

747
00:48:40,250 --> 00:48:43,003
[Diego] <i>I will never fall for that woman.</i>

748
00:48:43,086 --> 00:48:46,089
[Loring] <i>You're playing hide</i>
<i>and seek with your feelings!</i>

749
00:48:46,173 --> 00:48:48,133
-[Fernan] <i>True!</i>
-[laughter]

750
00:48:50,052 --> 00:48:53,305
<i>I shouldn't feel this way about</i>
<i>you because you're the enemy.</i>

751
00:48:54,139 --> 00:48:58,310
<i>But… why can't I get you off my mind?</i>

752
00:49:01,938 --> 00:49:04,483
<i>I heard your son, Diego,</i>
<i>tried to stop the project.</i>

753
00:49:04,566 --> 00:49:07,194
<i>Sorry to say, but</i>
<i>if you can't control your son,</i>

754
00:49:07,277 --> 00:49:08,695
<i>what more the people of Ardiente?</i>

755
00:49:08,779 --> 00:49:11,365
<i>I can't help but think</i>
<i>that if Grandpa were here,</i>

756
00:49:11,448 --> 00:49:13,700
<i>-we wouldn't be having problems.</i>
<i>-I'm the one here.</i>

757
00:49:13,784 --> 00:49:16,995
<i>And I'm more than capable</i>
<i>of solving these problems.</i>

758
00:49:17,079 --> 00:49:18,330
<i>-Wait!</i>
<i>-Miss Aguas! Miss Aguas!</i>

759
00:49:18,413 --> 00:49:20,374
<i>Mr. Mayor, make them stop.</i>
<i>There's a child here!</i>

760
00:49:20,457 --> 00:49:22,834
-<i>Have some mercy!</i>
-[screaming]

761
00:49:22,918 --> 00:49:25,295
[Diego] <i>You don't have a court</i>
<i>order because we all know</i>

762
00:49:25,379 --> 00:49:27,214
<i>this didn't go through the due process!</i>

763
00:49:27,297 --> 00:49:28,590
<i>The farmers will file an appeal!</i>

764
00:49:28,674 --> 00:49:29,841
[Emilia] <i>It's good that happened,</i>

765
00:49:29,925 --> 00:49:32,010
<i>so they get the message</i>

766
00:49:32,094 --> 00:49:35,013
<i>that they shouldn't be going</i>
<i>against the Ardientes.</i>

